---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
---
<Base title="Site guide — MQ CP Club" description="How the MQ CP Club website is built (work in progress).">
  <Header />
  <main class="mq-page">
    <a class="mono text-[13px] text-ink-muted no-underline" href="/contribute">← Contribute</a>
    <div class="mono mq-eyebrow mt-4">// SITE GUIDE</div>
    <h1 class="ps-h1 mq-h1-gap">How the website is built</h1>
    <p class="text-ink max-w-measure mt-3">
      A short tour of how the site is put together — which files hold what, and what to edit to
      change a given page.
    </p>

    <div class="ps-card mt-5 max-w-measure" style="border-top:3px solid var(--cat-3);">
      <div class="ps-card__title">🚧 Work in progress</div>
      <div class="ps-card__body">
        The site is still under active development, so the specifics here — file paths, structure,
        conventions — will change over the coming days. This page is a placeholder; check back
        soon for the full guide.
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="ps-h2 mq-heading mq-heading--mt7">What this will cover</h2>
    <ul class="text-ink max-w-measure leading-loose pl-5">
      <li>How Astro turns content files into pages — content collections plus page templates.</li>
      <li>Where each kind of content lives under <span class="mono">src/content/</span>, and how to add or edit it.</li>
      <li>Which file corresponds to which page.</li>
      <li>How to preview your changes locally before opening a pull request.</li>
    </ul>
  </main>
</Base>
